  when we did  uh but it was difficult it was really  difficult  it really when you look down the strip  in those days it was almost eerie and  think about each and every one of those  people as i know you do when you look  back at this year  what is something you are most proud of  and what is something if you could get a  do-over  uh a mulligan if you will something you  wish maybe a decision was made slightly  differently  as we kind of look in a retrospective  way yeah  the thing that and before i get to that  i want to say when what you said is true  when i drove down this trip i had my  detail my security take me on a  trip down the strip one time to go to  work more than once  and to see the eeriness of nobody on the  strip and nobody open  and you know it was difficult the thing  that i  am most proud of or i'm happiest about  is you saw the absolute best in people  through this pandemic and you saw the  worst in people through this pandemic  you had some folks that would not chose  not to comply with any of the directives  and didn't want to believe that believe  that coleman is a hoax  but at the same time you saw the best in  people you saw the nevada national guard  you saw them feeding people giving cove  a test  cleaning nursing homes uh giving covet  vaccines  delivering food delivering ppe they have  done absolutely everything we've asked  of them  all of the individuals that have donated  whether it's food whether it's money  whether it's their time  to help a neighbor that was in need if  they knew they had a senior citizen  living next door  they couldn't get out to buy if you  remember at the very beginning you  couldn't get toilet paper  wipes they don't they they went and got  it and brought it to their neighbors  that weren't so fortunate  that was uh really heartwarming to see  how much people  uh sacrificed and did for other people  uh the difficult parts the two parts  were  one uh when you deal with families of  those who have lost a loved one  and you know that that person couldn't  get in to say goodbye  you know when the person was dying and  they counted on a nurse  being with them to hold their hand to  face time with their family that's how  they got to say goodbye  that was difficult that's extremely  difficult that people had to go through  that and couldn't have a  a proper goodbye to a loved one couldn't  have a proper burial  for a loved one and people made an awful  lot of sacrifices to that extent  governor a lot of good news lately in  terms of cases plummeting especially in  the past six seven weeks  uh sporting events coming back if you  could clarify  with the fact that the governor's office  for nascar weekend and golden knights  games put capacity at 20  and it seemed to be reduced to 15 from  southern nevada health  district we heard from bill foley and  and chris powell and their frustration  with that wanting  the 20 that you talked about to be what  happens  can you explain what exactly happened  there sure i talked to bill  uh who i'm a big fan of both the golden  ice and the speedway has been a  tremendous thing for this community  uh we made a decision based on  our medical the medical advice i got our  science advice we got a business in  industry they looked at all the plans  all these  venues that they're going to put to  people in and i felt very very  comfortable going with 20  occupancy they could still be socially  distanced  uh they could still be safe i thought  for everybody involved  we made that uh part of a directive i  made that statement  and then the local jurisdictions whether  it's the  county or the city or the health  district said no we don't want to  give them 20 we only want to give them  15  i know there was a lot of frustration  with both chris and bill  as it related to that i understand their  frustration i know that they've had  people that have been waiting a year  to get into a race or to get into a  hockey game  and i understand that and uh like i say  i wanted 20  but the locals said that was they wanted  melt less so they ended up with less  governor more than half of a recent poll  supported your handling of the cobit  pandemic  over half were you uh as you look at the  43  that maybe did not how do you speak to  those that you're still trying to bring  on board  and what does it mean to you that over  have to approve of the job you've done  well i appreciate the fact that over  half approve of the job that we've done  it's not me it's  i've got to assemble the great team i  mean whether it's my staff here in  carson city with me or  what's the doctors and the medical  professionals or colvin task force  uh our profit advisory committee that  rolls out all this stuff  we're taking the best information we can  and moving forward  for the people that uh don't support  what i'm doing or how we're doing it  i understand that i still represent you  i still want to do the best i possibly  can  but some people just i understand that  they  most people think you should wear a mask  but they don't want to be told to wear a  mask  and i get that but i'm telling you it  works it makes a big big difference i  wish people would look at it  uh from the point of view if you don't  wear the mask for yourself as much as  you wear it for the people that you love  and the people you care about the people  you live with the people you work with  uh people you live near you know your  family members  and i would encourage everybody to  please do your part now is not the time  to let up and take your foot off the gas  so to speak  uh now is the time to double down and  continue as we get more and more people  vaccinated every day  we get thousands of more people of  accident  thousands of shots in people's arms so  every day it's getting a little bit  better  yeah then you just need people we need  to hold down for a couple more  uh months in order to get get where we  can get to that immunity of 80 to 90  then we'll be in 