he system so  much  uh with these fake claims and phony  claims  that it's really impacted legitimate  claimants so  i'm talking to my staff i think it's  important we do something about this and  this isn't 475 000  different people that put in claims this  is a group of syndicator  whatever you want to call it the that  are putting in  tens of thousands of claims and getting  all these cards and getting the benefits  and i think we need to take a bolder  step in terms of  investigating and prosecuting the  perpetrators of that because  they continue to put in fraudulent  claims they're not  questionable where you don't know if you  should get it you shouldn't get it  these are people putting claims that  have no rights to it they're putting in  multiple claims under different names  stealing identities it's just a really  sad situation  95 percent fraudulent question about  vaccinations  uh we are uh getting a lot of shots in  arms in nevada we did find out that  nevada's vaccine allocation rate was  using 24 to  2014 to 2018 census estimates which was  impacting the numbers  are you happy with the vaccination  process as of now and what do you want  to see different to improve it  well i'm happy but i can always be  happier we have a weekly call the  governor's association does with the  president's task force on vaccines every  week i look forward to the call because  every week they've upped our allocation  you know we're getting more and more and  more  it's unfortunate that they're using old  population estimates which  which kind of goddesses is it's hurting  the states that are getting more people  moving and it's helping the states that  people are moving out of  so that's a problem for that uh what i  want to see happen  and we're going to continue to expand  our sites  that are going to be made available to  go get vaccines uh i want to see more  and more of our elderly population  get the vaccine my mom's 94. she got  both of hers so i'm thrilled with that  she can feel safer but we need to get  our senior citizens vaccinated  and we need to do more in our minority  communities and we're going to we're  going to get into those communities our  are black and brown communities where  there's a little more hesitancy  to get the vaccine but i want to open  these up and give out every single dose  that we could possibly get coming our  way  and uh i think we're going to continue  to do that right now you've got  this many vaccines and this many people  want in the vaccine  but it's slowly starting to change when  we're going to have this many vaccines  and to wait out here  people that are going to be willing to  get them so we need to continue to  educate people  to encourage them to go and get the  vaccine and the first chance you'd get  to get an appointment get a vaccine i  don't care which one it is  if it's a needle with a vaccine they're  putting in your arm go get it we're all  going to be better off as a result  governor we appreciate your time glad to  hear your mom  94 years old got the vaccines is doing  well  and thank you so much for making time  for us here on eight news now we do  appreciate it

